Chicken Divan
  --Stephanie, the Cozy Cook

2 tbsp butter
2 lb.boneless skinless chicken breasts, see notes
salt/pepper, to taste
1 yellow onion, diced
1 rib celery, diced
4 c broccoli florets, ~1/2 lb
1 tbsp olive oil
10.5 oz cream of chicken soup
2/3 c sour cream
1/2 cup milk
1/2 tsp garlic powder
1/2 tsp onion powder
1/2 tsp mustard powder
2 1/2 c cheddar cheese, shredded

Preheat oven to 350F. Cut chicken into bite-sized pieces and sprinkle lightly with salt and pepper. Melt butter in a dutch oven or large pot over medium heat. Add the chicken, onions, and celery and toss to coat. Sauté for 3 min, until chicken is about halfway done, then add the broccoli and olive oil. Cook for 3-5 more min, until the chicken is cooked through. Remove from heat. Add the cream of chicken soup, sour cream, milk, seasonings, and half of the cheese. Stir to combine. Transfer to a lightly greased 9x13" casserole dish and top with remaining cheese. Cover and bake for 20 min. Remove and increase heat to 400F. 
  

Topping:
1/2 c crushed Ritz crackers, or panko breadcrumbs
2 tbsp butter

Combine the melted butter and Ritz crackers. Sprinkle over the casserole and bake for 8-10 min, until the top is golden brown. Remove and let it sit for 5 min prior to serving. Serve overv rice, biscuits, or mashed potatoes.


Notes: 2 lb chicken ~= 4 c, or 3 medium chicken breasts. can sub frozen broccoli; thaw first and pat dry. 1/2 c crushed Ritz ~= 14 or one sleeve.

  
